    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d811">

                <pb facs="0874" n="862" xml:id="pg862"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/754½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Lend-Lease Administrator</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Burns</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Acheson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-11-18">November 18,
                        1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Acheson</hi>: As you know, the
                    President, on November 7, 1941, found the defense of the Union of Soviet
                    Socialist Republics vital to the defense of the United States. Pursuant to this
                    finding, I am arranging to have defense articles transferred to the Soviet
                    Government as quickly as possible.</p>
                <p>The Soviet Government has already filed the necessary papers under Sections 4 and
                    7 of the Lend-Lease Act. It might be advisable, however, to obtain a formal
                    master agreement embodying the substance of the exchange of notes between the
                    President and Premier Stalin, the representations under Sections 4 and 7 of the
                    Lend-Lease Act and any other provisions deemed necessary or desirable.</p>
                <p>Very sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. H. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Burns</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
